they're allowed to explore that.

00:28:02.699 --> 00:28:04.899
-Would you say
it's a challenge for you here?

00:28:04.899 --> 00:28:05.793
-Oh, yeah.

00:28:05.793 --> 00:28:08.059
But it's...
[Peter chuckling]

00:28:08.059 --> 00:28:09.611
It's not something I can't do.

00:28:09.611 --> 00:28:11.030
It's for me...

00:28:11.030 --> 00:28:13.350
And this is just me speaking
from my perspective right now

00:28:13.350 --> 00:28:15.853
but it almost feels like
some level of enlightenment.

00:28:15.853 --> 00:28:18.591
Where once you get there
you can't go backwards

00:28:18.591 --> 00:28:22.076
and while polyamory is something
I never imagined in my whole life...

00:28:22.076 --> 00:28:25.192
I never even, like,
considered or thought of as real.

00:28:25.192 --> 00:28:28.994
I mean my great grandfather had a wife.

00:28:28.994 --> 00:28:30.675
Went away on a work campaign.

00:28:30.675 --> 00:28:32.853
Came back with a second wife and more kids

00:28:32.853 --> 00:28:35.060
and back then that was normal
in the Ottoman empire.

00:28:35.060 --> 00:28:38.394
The first wife poisoned
the second wife and the kids.

00:28:38.394 --> 00:28:40.773
That was my interpretation
of multiple wives.

00:28:40.773 --> 00:28:42.614
Is like, "That stuff happens."

00:28:42.614 --> 00:28:45.598
So I never even considered it a reality

00:28:45.598 --> 00:28:48.269
but being in the Bay Area

00:28:48.269 --> 00:28:50.222
