it's something you'll grow out of?

00:32:16.114 --> 00:32:17.357
You'll get older and you're like,

00:32:17.357 --> 00:32:18.859
"Ah, that doesn't interest me as much."

00:32:18.859 --> 00:32:20.024
-I think it's possible

00:32:20.024 --> 00:32:23.622
but at this point it doesn't seem like
it's something that's possible

00:32:23.622 --> 00:32:25.157
but who know?

00:32:26.095 --> 00:32:27.622
Ultimately, to me...

00:32:28.078 --> 00:32:30.192
Polyamory has been
really nice because one,

00:32:30.192 --> 00:32:33.962
I have a strong need
for adventure, curiosity, variety

00:32:33.962 --> 00:32:36.001
and on the other hand,
just need fulfillment.

00:32:36.001 --> 00:32:40.931
Like on the one hand I want somebody
really in the moment, playful, visual.

00:32:40.931 --> 00:32:44.030
Somebody that can be
a very similar opposite to me

00:32:44.030 --> 00:32:47.011
that I can appreciate
those parts of life through her

00:32:47.011 --> 00:32:50.325
but at the same time I also want
somebody who's sort of a partner in crime.

00:32:50.325 --> 00:32:52.274
Somebody who has
a similar alignment and vision

00:32:52.274 --> 00:32:55.694
and we can strategize
about a lot of subjects.

00:32:55.694 --> 00:32:57.869
I'm gonna go for the things that I want

00:32:57.869 --> 00:33:01.046
and if I'm not,
I'm just gonna be miserable.

00:33:02.910 --> 00:33:05.478
PETER: It's about staying true to yourself?
JOHN: Yeah.

00:33:05.478 --> 00:33:06.478
PETER: Keeping it real?

00:33:06.478 --> 00:33:09.121
JOHN: And if I'm not true to myself...

00:33:09.121 --> 00:33:12.204
Probably gonna cheat,
get divorced, have, like dark thoughts

00:33:12.204 --> 00:33:15.577
but having everything being
honest and open is

00:33:15.577 --> 00:33:18.447
I think, a much cleaner,
easier way to live.

00:33:20.607 --> 00:33:21.727
So what, um...

00:33:22.619 --> 00:33:27.485
Tell me about the journey you've had here
